cdex (0.0.1-11cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add 0018-start-menu-global-unfocus.patch: close the Start Menu when focus
    moves outside the menu hierarchy. Use a short timer on WM_ACTIVATEAPP
    deactivation, verify the real foreground window, and cancel the menu only
    if it does not belong to the menu itself, a submenu parent, the focus
    manager, or the taskbar. This makes the Start Menu close on a desktop
    click while keeping dropdown submenus usable.
  * Fix a CComPtr::operator& debug assertion in _IsSubMenuParent by using a
    temporary CComPtr when walking the submenu parent chain.

 -- Artem <artem@example.com>  Thu, 23 Jul 2026 19:40:02 +0300

