 -- Artem <artem@example.com>  Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:35:05 +0300

cdex (0.0.1-9cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add 0016-desktop-resize-on-displaychange.patch: defer the Program Manager
    resize out of the WM_DISPLAYCHANGE broadcast and retry on a timer until
    the work area becomes valid, so the desktop resizes to the new resolution
    and a resolution decrease no longer collapses it to a zero-size window.
  * Disable mscoree in create_reactos_shortcuts so Wine Mono Installer does
    not block the first login on a fresh prefix.
  * Set the desktop background color only once on prefix creation and ship it
    in the ChooseColor custom palette, instead of force-resetting it on every
    login, so the user's own choice persists.
  * Add 0017-save-resolution-on-displaychange.patch: persist the display
    resolution chosen in desk.cpl and re-apply it via xrandr early on login,
    so it survives the X server restarting at its default mode.
  * Depend on wine (>= 10.0.1-4cd), relaxed from an exact match so wine can
    be upgraded without leaving cdex-base in a broken state.

 -- Artem <artem@example.com>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:35:00 +0300

cdex (0.0.1-8cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Enlarge the UI font to match the global size:
    - WindowMetrics LOGFONT heights: caption/message/status -17,
      menu/icon/smcaption -14 (via ensure_reactos_ui_settings);
    - openbox title/menu fonts 8 -> 10 pt in openbox/rc.xml.
  * Add 0013-uxtheme-sysfont-fallback.patch and
    0014-uxtheme-getthemefont-unsupported.patch: the ReactOS uxtheme
    (native build) ignores .msstyles fonts; GetThemeSysFont falls back
    to the system (registry) fonts, GetThemeFont reports no per-part
    fonts so callers keep the DC (dialog/stock) font.
  * Add 0015-startbtn-no-text.patch: single-space caption for the
    icon-only start button, doubled width.
  * Add ensure_reactos_ui_settings and ensure_reactos_desktop_background:
    Winlogon\Shell, FontSubstitutes, font Replacements and WindowMetrics
    are separated from the desktop background color and re-applied via
    reg_add on every login, so wine.inf re-runs (after Wine upgrades) and
    theme applications can no longer clobber them.
  * Fix reg_add_logfont byte order: the LOGFONTW lfHeight field is
    little-endian, so the hex value passed to wine reg add must start
    with the least-significant byte (e.g. -17 -> EF FF FF FF).
  * Clean 0012-new-menu.patch format (drop a stray test hunk and the
    forbidden Index:/work.orig lines).
  * Depend on wine 10.0.1-3cd (larger DEFAULT_GUI_FONT, scaled dialog
    fonts, scoped Button/PUSHBUTTON label font).

 -- Artem <artem@example.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 21:00:00 +0300

cdex (0.0.1-7cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Vendor Ubuntu Font Family 0.83 (Regular/Bold/Regular-Italic) and patch
    it at build time: rewrite the GASP table so FreeType antialiases it at
    every size (tools/gasp_patch.py) and rename the family to
    "Ubuntu derivative CusDeb" per UFL 1.0 clause 2(c)
    (tools/rename_font.py, with LF_FACESIZE guard against wine stack
    smashing on long name strings).
  * Register the new family as the ReactOS/Wine UI font in
    reactos-registry.sh (desktop icons, taskbar, menus, dialogs).
  * Add fontconfig/52-cusdeb-ubuntu.conf so the Linux side (Openbox, GTK,
    LightDM greeter) also prefers the bundled family for sans-serif.

